WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:06.310
I'm doing some surveillance
on a slaughter farm

00:00:06.310 --> 00:00:07.223
Miami, Florida.

00:00:08.410 --> 00:00:11.400
On this farm they're
killing with sledgehammers,

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:12.633
and butchering alive.

00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:17.310
I think one of them saw me in the area,

00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:19.160
They patrol this area on ATVs.

00:00:23.296 --> 00:00:27.423
Threats have been made for
the past 13 years on my life.

00:00:31.166 --> 00:00:32.910
I'm not too popular in these areas.

00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:35.210
When they weren't chasing
me with sledgehammers

00:00:35.210 --> 00:00:38.170
and axes, I would be getting phone calls,

00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:39.340
I would be getting emails,

00:00:39.340 --> 00:00:41.740
I would be getting
messages on social media.

00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:42.980
An undercover operation

00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:45.410
sheds light into the
cruel treatment of animals

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:46.870
at a West Palm Beach farm.

00:00:46.870 --> 00:00:50.570
The animals behind us residing
in this torture operation

00:00:50.570 --> 00:00:51.910
have a voice today.

00:00:51.910 --> 00:00:53.420
When people would be arrested

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:55.420
in interrogation rooms,
they would tell law

00:00:55.420 --> 00:00:58.320
enforcement that guy, Kudo,
had better watch his ass

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:01.270
because there are bounties
on this guy's head.

00:01:01.270 --> 00:01:04.030
He's the only one taking
this industry down

00:01:04.030 --> 00:01:06.523
and no one wants that
person breathing anymore.

00:01:19.190 --> 00:01:21.650
So Richard Kudo is an interesting guy

00:01:21.650 --> 00:01:22.653
to say the least.

00:01:25.940 --> 00:01:28.173
So right now, we are in Area 97.

00:01:29.740 --> 00:01:31.630
We're just going over some mappings

00:01:31.630 --> 00:01:34.343
of some slaughter farms
and animal fighting farms.

00:01:35.460 --> 00:01:37.850
He sailed on the America's cup team

00:01:37.850 --> 00:01:39.800
like extreme sports guy.

00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:43.470
He was also a property flipper
in Miami, in South beach

00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:45.890
in the 2000s when the
market was quite high.

00:01:45.890 --> 00:01:49.230
And it's where I blossomed financially.

00:01:49.230 --> 00:01:52.760
It's where I made my money
and made my nest egg.

00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:54.350
But I had a void.

00:01:54.350 --> 00:01:59.003
I had a void of doing something
more important with my life.

00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:02.990
So Kudo was volunteering

00:02:02.990 --> 00:02:04.343
with the SPCA back in 2008.

00:02:08.650 --> 00:02:10.350
Basically mucking stalls,

00:02:10.350 --> 00:02:13.020
doing whatever work they
needed around the barn.

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:17.250
And they got a distress
call one day from the police

00:02:17.250 --> 00:02:19.840
because SPCA would often help relocate

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:22.960
animals that the police
would find in distress.

00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:26.300
So, you know, I went out
there driving my Range Rover

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:28.370
leaving South beach.

00:02:28.370 --> 00:02:31.890
And they came across some butchers farm

00:02:31.890 --> 00:02:32.723
that the police were at.

00:02:32.723 --> 00:02:35.430
They came across this
horse, beautiful horse

00:02:35.430 --> 00:02:37.077
brown with white on his nose.

00:02:37.077 --> 00:02:40.700
He had a broken leg, he was emaciated.

00:02:40.700 --> 00:02:43.510
And I walked up to him and he put his head

00:02:43.510 --> 00:02:46.580
in my arms and he just
put all his weight on me.

00:02:46.580 --> 00:02:50.040
And right then and there, I
started falling for this animal

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:53.670
But underneath the horses lip

00:02:53.670 --> 00:02:56.760
on its gums was tattooed a code.

00:02:56.760 --> 00:02:59.703
And they were kind of curious
to know what that meant.

00:03:02.290 --> 00:03:04.010
It turns out that these
horses are tattooed

00:03:04.010 --> 00:03:06.150
on their lips to show where they're from

00:03:06.150 --> 00:03:08.450
and what their pedigree
is and they belong to.

00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:13.973
And so this horse, this horse
is named Freedom's Flight.

00:03:13.973 --> 00:03:17.240
The horse had broken
its leg during a race.

00:03:17.240 --> 00:03:22.210
So I tracked his lineage
and it was shocking

00:03:22.210 --> 00:03:24.690
that I learned of his
bloodlines, that it came

00:03:24.690 --> 00:03:28.160
from some of the most famous
race horses on the planet.

00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:33.060
How could this horse end up
at an illegal slaughterhouse?

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:34.593
It boggled my mind.

00:03:36.370 --> 00:03:38.180
He ended up adopting him.

00:03:38.180 --> 00:03:40.880
Freedom Flight still lives
at his compound in Florida.

00:03:41.950 --> 00:03:43.740
Sort of got him going into this world

00:03:43.740 --> 00:03:45.483
of underground horse butchering.

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:53.290
These are slaughter horses here.

00:03:53.290 --> 00:03:55.050
And we have a mayor down here.

00:03:55.050 --> 00:03:56.700
She's clinging to life right now.

00:03:57.780 --> 00:04:01.000
The SPCA was not an
organization that was geared

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:04.230
towards me or anyone else going undercover

00:04:04.230 --> 00:04:06.600
and investigating these people, which is

00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:09.920
the only reason why I started
the animal recovery mission.

00:04:09.920 --> 00:04:11.320
The animal recovery mission

00:04:11.320 --> 00:04:12.980
taped and exposed the property

00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:15.470
while conducting an investigation.

00:04:15.470 --> 00:04:19.783
We basically go undercover
where no one else will.

00:04:22.410 --> 00:04:24.670
And the public sector
and the private sector,

00:04:24.670 --> 00:04:25.980
if they're disregarding something

00:04:25.980 --> 00:04:29.883
as far as animal cruelty
ARM will take it on.

00:04:31.280 --> 00:04:35.050
It's something that is
so incredibly important

00:04:35.050 --> 00:04:37.810
and it's become my life's mission.

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:39.010
He's so skinny.

00:04:39.010 --> 00:04:43.180
I would just cut checks and
rip out my bank accounts

00:04:43.180 --> 00:04:45.550
to fund it without thinking about it.

00:04:45.550 --> 00:04:49.370
The guy right here, his
wife who sort of up.

00:04:49.370 --> 00:04:51.390
And to be honest I don't
know how much money

00:04:51.390 --> 00:04:55.550
that I've spent, but it's
close to the seven figures over

00:04:55.550 --> 00:04:56.490
and

00:04:58.555 --> 00:04:59.643
it's been worth it.

00:05:00.750 --> 00:05:05.460
I'm dealing with the USDA
right now on a horse meat buy.

00:05:05.460 --> 00:05:08.060
Basically they're embedded
with some horse killers.

00:05:08.060 --> 00:05:11.350
So horse meat internationally
is a pretty commonly

00:05:11.350 --> 00:05:13.750
eaten food, not on the
level of beef or pork

00:05:14.810 --> 00:05:17.690
but it's popular in a
lot of cultures in Japan,

00:05:17.690 --> 00:05:20.620
central Asia, France, and in Cuba.

00:05:20.620 --> 00:05:23.520
And a lot of Cuban-Americans
live in South Florida.

00:05:23.520 --> 00:05:26.913
And many of them still
want to eat horse meat.

00:05:29.670 --> 00:05:32.380
They're eating horse meat
for medical purposes.

00:05:32.380 --> 00:05:35.210
They think that it cures blood disorders

00:05:35.210 --> 00:05:38.290
that it helps with side
effects from chemotherapy.

00:05:38.290 --> 00:05:41.790
But all horse meat, whether it's imported

00:05:41.790 --> 00:05:44.790
or horses are slaughtered and butchered

00:05:44.790 --> 00:05:49.010
in this country for human
consumption, it's illegal.

00:05:49.010 --> 00:05:51.800
This is roughly 30 pounds
of horse meat purchased

00:05:51.800 --> 00:05:53.760
in Palm beach County.

00:05:53.760 --> 00:05:55.810
They've actually cut this horse meat

00:05:55.810 --> 00:05:57.923
into small steak-like filets.

00:06:03.080 --> 00:06:06.820
In Florida, the problem is that many times

00:06:06.820 --> 00:06:11.820
laws geared towards protecting
animals are not being upheld

00:06:12.410 --> 00:06:16.470
by law enforcement,
prosecutors, judges, and juries.

00:06:16.470 --> 00:06:20.223
And that's extremely,
extremely frustrating.

00:06:21.320 --> 00:06:24.320
The laws in Florida are still too weak.

00:06:24.320 --> 00:06:29.320
If you are a first time
felony animal abuser

00:06:29.380 --> 00:06:32.580
it is unlikely that you
will get prison time.

00:06:32.580 --> 00:06:34.970
You may get County jail time

00:06:35.890 --> 00:06:40.290
but that even would be
in some cases, a stretch.

00:06:40.290 --> 00:06:43.080
There's really not a whole
lot I can do with them

00:06:43.080 --> 00:06:46.280
whether they plead guilty
or they're found guilty

00:06:46.280 --> 00:06:49.970
because most judges, even
in the most horrible crimes

00:06:49.970 --> 00:06:52.920
do not put them in jail
will not put them in prison.

00:06:52.920 --> 00:06:55.083
So they're placed on probation.

00:06:56.110 --> 00:06:58.840
Animal abuse here is so under reported

00:06:58.840 --> 00:07:01.570
because there simply are not the resources

00:07:01.570 --> 00:07:05.010
for the police departments,
the Sheriff's department,

00:07:05.010 --> 00:07:07.277
animal care and control to go out

00:07:07.277 --> 00:07:09.563
and really investigate these crimes.

00:07:15.320 --> 00:07:17.400
Right now I'm in the C-9 Basin

00:07:17.400 --> 00:07:18.930
a really nasty property

00:07:18.930 --> 00:07:21.503
with four completely emaciated horses.

00:07:23.710 --> 00:07:27.450
The C-9 Basin is this patch of brushy land

00:07:27.450 --> 00:07:30.320
wedged between Miami and the Everglades.

00:07:30.320 --> 00:07:32.870
And it's really meant to be
an ecological buffer zone.

00:07:32.870 --> 00:07:35.970
It's not really meant to
have humans living there

00:07:35.970 --> 00:07:37.703
but lots of people do live there.

00:07:38.609 --> 00:07:40.853
There are the horses.

00:07:40.853 --> 00:07:43.070
This is the kill area here.

00:07:43.070 --> 00:07:45.670
That's the rug that they're
covering the horses with

00:07:45.670 --> 00:07:47.323
after they remove the meat.

00:07:49.040 --> 00:07:51.050
When I first started
investigating the basin

00:07:51.050 --> 00:07:53.300
at the beginning of 2009,

00:07:53.300 --> 00:07:55.670
law enforcement wouldn't
even go into the basin

00:07:55.670 --> 00:07:59.790
no one would go into the
basin and uphold laws.

00:07:59.790 --> 00:08:02.380
Certainly wouldn't go in
there to investigate crimes

00:08:02.380 --> 00:08:06.240
against animals, which was
why horse meat was flourishing

00:08:06.240 --> 00:08:07.073
as an industry.

00:08:09.030 --> 00:08:11.950
This area is pretty lawless.

00:08:11.950 --> 00:08:14.560
A local paper in Miami
called it the closest thing

00:08:14.560 --> 00:08:16.830
America has to a wild West outpost

00:08:16.830 --> 00:08:18.520
and having been there a couple of times

00:08:18.520 --> 00:08:20.793
I can attest to that being true.

00:08:24.060 --> 00:08:27.343
And then people's pet
horses start being stolen.

00:08:31.080 --> 00:08:33.200
Usually someone's pet horse, their pony,

00:08:33.200 --> 00:08:34.920
they'll come to the barn in the morning

00:08:34.920 --> 00:08:36.830
and either the horse has vanished

00:08:36.830 --> 00:08:40.510
or a couple of hundred yards
away and a trail of blood away

00:08:40.510 --> 00:08:43.200
there's a perfectly butchered
and filleted carcass

00:08:43.200 --> 00:08:45.480
of what used to be your pet pony.

00:08:45.480 --> 00:08:48.730
When was my horse
stolen, he was butchered.

00:08:48.730 --> 00:08:50.690
He was tied into a palm tree.

00:08:50.690 --> 00:08:52.260
So all these are bloodstains here?

00:08:52.260 --> 00:08:53.270
Yeah.

00:08:53.270 --> 00:08:58.030
When I started going in
to the basin in 2009,

00:08:58.030 --> 00:09:01.530
I was still a developer, but
I knew hundreds of thousands

00:09:01.530 --> 00:09:04.050
of animals were in there being brutalized

00:09:04.050 --> 00:09:08.153
with everyone ignoring
the crimes against them.

00:09:09.050 --> 00:09:11.430
Animals were killed in
really inhumane ways,

00:09:11.430 --> 00:09:14.410
being stabbed in the chest or
shot with low caliber guns,

00:09:14.410 --> 00:09:17.360
their throat sled and
tortured, boiled alive,

00:09:17.360 --> 00:09:18.420
really horrific stuff.

00:09:18.420 --> 00:09:20.020
And to see his videos,

00:09:20.020 --> 00:09:22.710
he has a massive trove
of undercover videos

00:09:22.710 --> 00:09:24.243
is pretty scary stuff.

00:09:25.380 --> 00:09:26.580
So this is Kudo Thawn.

00:09:27.680 --> 00:09:31.483
I am investigating an
illegal slaughter farm.

00:09:31.483 --> 00:09:33.333
I didn't know what I was doing,

00:09:33.333 --> 00:09:35.400
completely and utterly untrained.

00:09:35.400 --> 00:09:39.463
I am armed but I still
don't feel that safe.

00:09:42.040 --> 00:09:45.720
And I started to infiltrate properties.

00:09:45.720 --> 00:09:48.440
Some of them legally,
some of them illegally.

00:09:48.440 --> 00:09:53.100
And I started to document the
crimes against the animals.

00:09:53.100 --> 00:09:56.650
See a horse. Doesn't look
like he's in great shape.

00:09:56.650 --> 00:09:57.500
Before he got involved,

00:09:57.500 --> 00:10:00.680
there really wasn't a lot
of policing of this world.

00:10:00.680 --> 00:10:03.570
The police down there
have a lot on their plates

00:10:03.570 --> 00:10:07.380
in terms of the murder and
robbery and credit card fraud.

00:10:07.380 --> 00:10:09.430
And so animal cruelty was not really high

00:10:09.430 --> 00:10:11.310
on their list of priorities.

00:10:11.310 --> 00:10:15.280
I think that when you have
a state where animal cruelty

00:10:15.280 --> 00:10:18.490
is way too prevalent, and
our laws are way too weak,

00:10:18.490 --> 00:10:21.810
it's important to have someone
like Richard Kudo out there.

00:10:21.810 --> 00:10:25.470
He's someone who's a true
believer, who takes risks

00:10:25.470 --> 00:10:30.200
and sometimes crossing the
line to get these secret videos

00:10:30.200 --> 00:10:31.263
out to the public.

00:10:32.270 --> 00:10:37.250
I understand his passion behind it

00:10:37.250 --> 00:10:41.780
but the way he goes
about it, is not the way

00:10:41.780 --> 00:10:44.180
one should go about it if
you're going to successfully

00:10:44.180 --> 00:10:47.350
prosecute these animal cruelty cases.

00:10:47.350 --> 00:10:50.720
I investigated the C-9
Basin for roughly six months

00:10:50.720 --> 00:10:55.310
and I comprised files of
roughly a hundred properties,

00:10:55.310 --> 00:10:58.580
illegal properties, and I
presented it to law enforcement

00:10:58.580 --> 00:11:02.570
but I also collected
violations, building violations,

00:11:02.570 --> 00:11:05.990
zoning violations,
environmental violations

00:11:05.990 --> 00:11:09.470
while I was collecting
crimes against animals.

00:11:09.470 --> 00:11:11.420
Just come out of this one farm now.

00:11:11.420 --> 00:11:16.080
And after roughly six months
of just about every night

00:11:16.080 --> 00:11:19.230
infiltrating every single
property that I possibly

00:11:19.230 --> 00:11:22.310
could in the basin, I created a report.

00:11:22.310 --> 00:11:24.740
And the police, they're shocked

00:11:24.740 --> 00:11:26.368
by what's going on in the Basin

00:11:26.368 --> 00:11:28.210
not only from an animal rights perspective

00:11:28.210 --> 00:11:30.903
but also from a zoning
and codes perspective.

00:11:33.420 --> 00:11:34.810
And the investigation

00:11:34.810 --> 00:11:39.583
of the C-9 Basin actually
led to Operation Restore.

00:11:42.230 --> 00:11:45.600
And it was one of the largest operations

00:11:45.600 --> 00:11:47.750
in history of the state of Florida.

00:11:47.750 --> 00:11:49.410
Thousands of agents

00:11:49.410 --> 00:11:53.770
tactically hitting the entire C-9 Basin

00:11:53.770 --> 00:11:54.890
Just after dawn

00:11:54.890 --> 00:11:56.700
an army of regulators and police

00:11:56.700 --> 00:11:59.520
deployed to shut down slaughter farms.

00:11:59.520 --> 00:12:01.070
It was just a massive take-down

00:12:01.070 --> 00:12:04.700
of illegal activity that was
going on in the C-9 Basin.

00:12:04.700 --> 00:12:09.190
17 cockfighting rings, over
400 illegal structures.

00:12:09.190 --> 00:12:10.760
You know, hundreds of citations issued

00:12:10.760 --> 00:12:13.430
for dumping and butchering
an animal cruelty.

00:12:13.430 --> 00:12:16.703
It was the most incredible
thing that I had ever seen.

00:12:17.590 --> 00:12:21.860
And all of those nights
infiltrating these properties,

00:12:21.860 --> 00:12:24.790
all of those nights,
being chased with machetes

00:12:24.790 --> 00:12:27.713
and axes, the danger that I put myself in,

00:12:29.570 --> 00:12:31.740
it paid off.

00:12:31.740 --> 00:12:34.460
So after the raid, governor Charlie Crist

00:12:34.460 --> 00:12:37.440
signs a law that basically
increases penalties

00:12:37.440 --> 00:12:39.570
for slaughtering horses.

00:12:39.570 --> 00:12:42.430
And to Kudo, this seems like it should be

00:12:42.430 --> 00:12:44.396
the end of the story, a sort of climax

00:12:44.396 --> 00:12:48.083
and it's actually the end
of act one in the story.

00:12:54.840 --> 00:12:57.461
So kudos on a high,

00:12:57.461 --> 00:13:01.420
you can almost hear
the happy music playing

00:13:01.420 --> 00:13:04.740
as he's awarded citizen of the
year by the Miami new times

00:13:04.740 --> 00:13:07.380
but he starts becoming more paranoid

00:13:07.380 --> 00:13:09.163
about the enemies that he's making.

00:13:11.170 --> 00:13:13.920
Butchers do not like him,
they have followed him,

00:13:13.920 --> 00:13:15.350
they have shot at him.

00:13:15.350 --> 00:13:17.260
Kill buyers, people all over the country

00:13:17.260 --> 00:13:21.050
who are buying horses to
export for meat don't like him.

00:13:21.050 --> 00:13:24.270
And so his paranoia was
actually quite justified.

00:13:24.270 --> 00:13:27.350
All these mofos know who
I am and what I look like

00:13:27.350 --> 00:13:30.373
and they don't like me.

00:13:31.650 --> 00:13:32.810
There was one year

00:13:32.810 --> 00:13:36.540
I believe I moved close
to seven different times

00:13:36.540 --> 00:13:39.800
because they were finding
my address in utilities.

00:13:39.800 --> 00:13:41.280
When I would put my name

00:13:41.280 --> 00:13:44.770
under an electric bill or a cable bill

00:13:44.770 --> 00:13:47.487
The police, and the local
authorities were kind of like,

00:13:47.487 --> 00:13:48.790
"All right, we've made some arrests.

00:13:48.790 --> 00:13:52.740
We did some enforcement. Let's
move on to other topics."

00:13:52.740 --> 00:13:54.620
Whereas he wasn't able to let it go.

00:13:54.620 --> 00:13:58.360
I wasn't looking in the
past, in my accomplishments

00:13:58.360 --> 00:14:01.963
I was looking at the future of
what still needed to be done.

00:14:02.880 --> 00:14:05.100
So after the raid he begins fundraising

00:14:05.100 --> 00:14:06.520
quite aggressively.

00:14:06.520 --> 00:14:08.040
And in addition to being very good

00:14:08.040 --> 00:14:09.520
at garnering media attention

00:14:09.520 --> 00:14:12.170
he's very good at
opening people's wallets.

00:14:12.170 --> 00:14:14.177
And he goes from 100,000 to 200,000

00:14:14.177 --> 00:14:17.720
to 500,000 to several
million dollars a year

00:14:17.720 --> 00:14:21.300
in annual income from donations.

00:14:21.300 --> 00:14:23.580
Undercover video of
animal cruelty captured

00:14:23.580 --> 00:14:27.120
at a popular farm in Northwest
Indiana is under review.

00:14:27.120 --> 00:14:28.720
He starts doing undercover operations

00:14:28.720 --> 00:14:31.870
in Indiana and other states, abroad

00:14:31.870 --> 00:14:34.160
and in Asia, looking at
animal cruelty there.

00:14:34.160 --> 00:14:36.087
Greetings from Bangladesh.

00:14:36.087 --> 00:14:38.170
And the vision is that
from the springboard

00:14:38.170 --> 00:14:43.170
of the C-9 basin, he catapults
into much larger operations.

00:14:43.630 --> 00:14:46.360
But what he doesn't realize
is that the C-9 basin story

00:14:46.360 --> 00:14:47.713
is not finished at all.

00:14:55.080 --> 00:14:57.330
We went to the C-9 Basin at Christmas time

00:14:57.330 --> 00:14:58.163
two years ago

00:14:59.490 --> 00:15:03.730
and we saw a blacked out fence

00:15:03.730 --> 00:15:05.620
and heard animals screaming

00:15:05.620 --> 00:15:07.830
and knew that that was slaughter house

00:15:07.830 --> 00:15:08.883
so we walked in.

00:15:10.000 --> 00:15:12.950
And sure enough, they were
butchering every animal

00:15:12.950 --> 00:15:14.940
you could imagine alive.

00:15:14.940 --> 00:15:18.420
Goats, sheep, pigs, birds.

00:15:18.420 --> 00:15:20.980
So we started to buy at
pigs and goats for meat

00:15:20.980 --> 00:15:22.890
for human consumption.

00:15:22.890 --> 00:15:24.960
Then we started purchasing horse meat.

00:15:24.960 --> 00:15:27.270
And this took back and forth.

00:15:27.270 --> 00:15:28.550
We're talking two years.

00:15:28.550 --> 00:15:33.170
This is a long investigation
called Operation Genesis.

00:15:33.170 --> 00:15:35.890
They start building a case file

00:15:35.890 --> 00:15:38.083
against the owner of the farm.

00:15:39.230 --> 00:15:40.743
Oh yeah. There it is.
It's a little chop it up,

00:15:42.500 --> 00:15:44.080
put in these bags.

00:15:44.080 --> 00:15:49.080
And in November, 2020, Kudo
invited me down to Florida

00:15:49.190 --> 00:15:51.733
to be part of the raid
on the slaughter house.

00:15:56.830 --> 00:15:58.520
Last night, the department
of health announced

00:15:58.520 --> 00:16:01.350
that there were two
presumptive positive cases

00:16:01.350 --> 00:16:04.900
of Corona virus disease
in the state of Florida.

00:16:04.900 --> 00:16:08.130
So the pandemic hit in March

00:16:08.130 --> 00:16:11.950
about a week after I was
in South Florida with Kudo.

00:16:11.950 --> 00:16:15.530
And this really put a hamper on his plans.

00:16:15.530 --> 00:16:18.340
I had to pull my investigators
out of the field.

00:16:18.340 --> 00:16:20.010
Months and months later,

00:16:20.010 --> 00:16:23.250
we went back and forth with
emails with law enforcement.

00:16:23.250 --> 00:16:26.320
And I got a very bad
feeling that law enforcement

00:16:26.320 --> 00:16:29.350
did not want this case for some reason.

00:16:29.350 --> 00:16:32.380
The plan was basically
kind of a hail Mary.

00:16:32.380 --> 00:16:35.360
They were going to go
under cover that morning,

00:16:35.360 --> 00:16:38.690
bring some evidence out and then call 911.

00:16:38.690 --> 00:16:41.830
We called 911, law enforcement responded

00:16:41.830 --> 00:16:45.570
and gave excuses on why
they couldn't make arrests.

00:16:45.570 --> 00:16:48.300
The police immediately knew who Kudo was.

00:16:48.300 --> 00:16:52.280
You could see how
annoyed they were at him.

00:16:52.280 --> 00:16:54.840
And you could see that they
really didn't want to be there.

00:16:54.840 --> 00:16:57.950
So they wrote up some
notes, they open a case file

00:16:57.950 --> 00:16:59.780
and they basically told us to get lost.

00:16:59.780 --> 00:17:02.980
When it's disregarded,
you throw up your hands,

00:17:02.980 --> 00:17:06.670
you let out a sigh, you're
you're so disheartened,

00:17:06.670 --> 00:17:09.060
you question your tactics.

00:17:09.060 --> 00:17:10.230
Should I have brought this case

00:17:10.230 --> 00:17:12.460
to law enforcement to begin with?

00:17:12.460 --> 00:17:14.640
I think someone who's out
there to hold accountable

00:17:14.640 --> 00:17:17.690
the worst of the animal
abusers is a good thing.

00:17:17.690 --> 00:17:20.240
It's just that sometimes
we can't use his evidence

00:17:20.240 --> 00:17:22.100
because it doesn't meet the standards

00:17:22.100 --> 00:17:23.837
of admissibility in a courtroom.

00:17:23.837 --> 00:17:28.170
You cannot just go in and
film people or record people.

00:17:28.170 --> 00:17:30.390
We do have laws on that.

00:17:30.390 --> 00:17:33.497
No matter what you see, what you hear

00:17:33.497 --> 00:17:37.060
you cannot as a private
citizen, film people,

00:17:37.060 --> 00:17:40.280
record people without their
consent in the state of Florida.

00:17:40.280 --> 00:17:44.420
And you cannot continually
go in and have them

00:17:44.420 --> 00:17:46.350
slaughter an animal in front of you

00:17:46.350 --> 00:17:48.810
just so you can film what they're doing.

00:17:48.810 --> 00:17:50.210
Over the years over the last decade,

00:17:50.210 --> 00:17:52.430
their patience has grown increasingly thin

00:17:52.430 --> 00:17:54.020
to the point where now,

00:17:54.020 --> 00:17:57.200
they say they want to work with him

00:17:57.200 --> 00:17:59.750
but they give very little indication

00:17:59.750 --> 00:18:01.150
that that's actually true.

00:18:01.150 --> 00:18:04.630
It seems like they really
would like him to go away.

00:18:04.630 --> 00:18:08.210
You question everything about yourself.

00:18:08.210 --> 00:18:10.050
about your organization.

00:18:10.050 --> 00:18:12.530
Are you really making an impact?

00:18:12.530 --> 00:18:14.583
Are you really helping animals?

00:18:19.980 --> 00:18:24.980
I created ARM to create
change no matter what.

00:18:25.150 --> 00:18:27.230
I'm not here to make
friends with prosecutors,

00:18:27.230 --> 00:18:29.720
or law enforcement or anyone else.

00:18:29.720 --> 00:18:32.143
I'm just here to help
animals and that's it.

00:18:33.010 --> 00:18:33.843
That's the difference

00:18:33.843 --> 00:18:35.500
between being an activist
and a prosecutor.

00:18:35.500 --> 00:18:37.730
Being an activist is to make a point

00:18:37.730 --> 00:18:40.330
and being a prosecutor is to do justice.

00:18:40.330 --> 00:18:41.500
And you can only do justice

00:18:41.500 --> 00:18:46.000
within the confines of the
courtroom with rules of evidence.

00:18:46.000 --> 00:18:47.350
So I guess you have to ask yourself

00:18:47.350 --> 00:18:48.490
do you want to make a point

00:18:48.490 --> 00:18:50.270
or do you want to make a difference?

00:18:50.270 --> 00:18:51.470
Working with law enforcement

00:18:51.470 --> 00:18:54.710
and government has very
little meaning to me.

00:18:54.710 --> 00:18:58.230
My main goal in ARM now is to educate.

00:18:58.230 --> 00:19:00.570
At times even change diets

00:19:00.570 --> 00:19:02.780
because if people didn't eat meat,

00:19:02.780 --> 00:19:04.350
then there wouldn't be these markets

00:19:04.350 --> 00:19:05.810
for me to investigate.

00:19:05.810 --> 00:19:08.000
They would not exist.

00:19:08.000 --> 00:19:11.493
I will never ever give up.

00:19:11.493 --> 00:19:14.270
I strive to make change
and to help animals

00:19:14.270 --> 00:19:18.470
and live a good, decent,
ethical life for them.

